{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Elohim, I seek You</b> — like one who seeks good, or from the root שחר like ולבקר בהיכלו from the root בקר." "<b>My soul thirsts for You</b> — my soul is like one who thirsts for water and my flesh is dry, for there is no word paired with כמה in Scripture." "<b>In a land</b> — as though I were in a land of dryness where there is no water and a weary land, for ארץ is found as masculine, נעתם ארץ, and there are many like it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {2 "The phrase נעתם ארץ is opaque; possibly a citation or example of ארץ construed as masculine. Translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:35.294730664Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}